---
import StandardLayout from '../../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import LegalShell from '../../components/LegalShell.astro';
import { localizedPath } from '../../i18n';

// ⚠️ COURTESY TRANSLATION of src/pages/fr/charte-de-confidentialite.astro —
// to be reviewed by legal counsel before going live. French law remains the
// applicable law and the French version prevails (stated on the page).

const toc = [
  { href: '#intro', label: '1. Definition and nature of personal data' },
  { href: '#rcp', label: '2. Purpose of this privacy policy' },
  { href: '#cnil', label: '3. Identity of the data controller' },
  { href: '#collecte', label: '4. Collection of personal data' },
  { href: '#destinataires', label: '5. Recipients of the collected data' },
  { href: '#conservation', label: '6. Retention period of personal data' },
  { href: '#identite', label: '7. Regarding identity documents' },
  { href: '#cartes', label: '8. Regarding payment card data' },
  { href: '#statistiques', label: '9. Regarding audience measurement statistics' },
  { href: '#securite', label: '10. Security' },
  { href: '#cookies', label: '11. Cookies' },
  { href: '#consentement', label: '12. Consent' },
  { href: '#donnees', label: '13. Access to your personal data' },
  { href: '#modifications', label: '14. Changes' },
  { href: '#date', label: '15. Effective date' },
] as const;
---

<StandardLayout market="en" routeKey="privacy" title="Privacy policy">
  <LegalShell market="en" title="Privacy policy" toc={toc}>
    <p>
      <em>
        This English version is provided for convenience only. The&nbsp;
        <a href={localizedPath('privacy', 'fr')}>French version</a> is the legally binding one.
      </em>
    </p>

    <section id="intro">
      <h2>1. Definition and nature of personal data</h2>
      <p>While you use our site, we may ask you to provide us with personal data about yourself.</p>
      <p>The term “personal data” refers to any data that makes it possible to identify an individual, which notably includes your surname, first names, username, photograph, postal and email addresses, phone numbers, date of birth, data relating to your transactions on the site, details of your purchases and subscriptions, payment card numbers, as well as any other information you choose to share with us about yourself.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="rcp">
      <h2>2. Purpose of this privacy policy</h2>
      <p>The purpose of this policy is to inform you about the means we use to collect your personal data, in the strictest respect of your rights.</p>
      <p>In this regard, we inform you that, in collecting and managing your personal data, we comply with French law no. 78-17 of 6 January 1978 on information technology, files and civil liberties, in its current version.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cnil">
      <h2>3. Identity of the data controller</h2>
      <p>The controller of your personal data is IZIKA SAS (a French simplified joint-stock company), registered with the Montpellier Trade and Companies Register under no. 807 746 524, with its registered office at 199 rue Hélène Boucher, 34170 Castelnau-le-Lez, France.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="collecte">
      <h2>4. Collection of personal data</h2>
      <p>Your personal data is collected for one or more of the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Managing your access to and use of certain services available on the websites,</li>
        <li>Carrying out customer management operations regarding contracts, orders, deliveries, invoices, loyalty programmes and customer relationship follow-up,</li>
        <li>Building a file of registered members, users, customers and prospects,</li>
        <li>Sending newsletters, solicitations and promotional messages. If you do not wish to receive them, we give you the option to object at the time your data is collected;</li>
        <li>Compiling commercial and traffic statistics for our services,</li>
        <li>Organising contests, sweepstakes and any promotional operations, excluding online gambling and games of chance subject to approval by the French Online Gaming Regulatory Authority,</li>
        <li>Managing user reviews of products, services or content,</li>
        <li>Managing unpaid invoices and any disputes relating to the use of our products and services,</li>
        <li>Complying with our legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
        <li>When collecting your personal data, we inform you whether certain data must be provided or is optional. We also inform you of the possible consequences of not providing it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="destinataires">
      <h2>5. Recipients of the collected data</h2>
      <p>Our company's staff, the departments in charge of auditing (statutory auditors in particular) and our processors will have access to your personal data.</p>
      <p>Public bodies may also receive your personal data, exclusively to meet our legal obligations, as may judicial officers, ministerial officers and debt collection agencies.</p>
      <p>Transfer of personal data<br />Your personal data will not be sold, rented or exchanged for the benefit of third parties.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="conservation">
      <h2>6. Retention period of personal data</h2>
      <p>Regarding data relating to customer and prospect management:<br />Your personal data will not be kept beyond the period strictly necessary to manage our commercial relationship with you. However, data establishing proof of a right or contract, which must be kept to comply with a legal obligation, will be retained for the period provided by applicable law.</p>
      <p>Regarding any marketing operations towards customers, their data may be kept for three years from the end of the commercial relationship.</p>
      <p>Personal data relating to a prospect who is not a customer may be kept for three years from its collection or from the prospect's last contact.</p>
      <p>At the end of this three-year period, we may contact you again to find out whether you wish to keep receiving commercial solicitations.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="identite">
      <h2>7. Regarding identity documents</h2>
      <p>If the right of access or rectification is exercised, data relating to identity documents may be kept for the period provided for in Article 9 of the French Code of Criminal Procedure, i.e. one year. If the right to object is exercised, this data may be archived for the limitation period provided for in Article 8 of the French Code of Criminal Procedure, i.e. three years.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cartes">
      <h2>8. Regarding payment card data</h2>
      <p>Financial transactions relating to the payment of purchases and fees via the site are entrusted to a payment service provider which ensures their proper execution and security.</p>
      <p>For the needs of the services, this payment service provider may receive your personal data relating to your payment card numbers, which it collects and stores in our name and on our behalf.</p>
      <p>We do not have access to this data.</p>
      <p>To allow you to make regular purchases or pay the related fees on the site, your payment card data is kept for as long as you remain registered on the site and at least until you complete your last transaction.</p>
      <p>By ticking the box expressly provided for this purpose on the site, you give us your express consent to this retention.</p>
      <p>The data relating to the visual cryptogram or CVV2 shown on your payment card is not stored.</p>
      <p>If you refuse to let your personal data relating to your payment card numbers be kept under the conditions described above, we will not keep this data beyond the time needed to complete the transaction.</p>
      <p>In any event, this data may be kept, as intermediate archives, for evidentiary purposes in case of a possible dispute over the transaction, for the period provided for by Article L 133-24 of the French Monetary and Financial Code — in this case 13 months following the debit date. This period may be extended to 15 months to account for the possible use of deferred-debit payment cards.</p>
      <p>Regarding the management of opt-out lists for marketing:<br />The information needed to honour your right to object is kept for at least three years from the exercise of that right.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="statistiques">
      <h2>9. Regarding audience measurement statistics</h2>
      <p>Information stored in users' devices, or any other element used to identify users and enable their traceability or attendance tracking, will not be kept beyond 12 months.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="securite">
      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>We inform you that we take all useful precautions and appropriate organisational and technical measures to preserve the security, integrity and confidentiality of your personal data and, in particular, to prevent it from being altered or damaged and to prevent unauthorised third parties from accessing it. We also use, or may use, secure payment systems consistent with the state of the art and the applicable regulations.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies">
      <h2>11. Cookies</h2>
      <p>Cookies are text files, often encrypted, stored in your browser. They are created when a user's browser loads a given website: the site sends information to the browser, which then creates a text file. Each time the user returns to the same site, the browser retrieves this file and sends it to the website's server.</p>
      <p>Two types of cookies, with different purposes, can be distinguished: technical cookies and advertising cookies:</p>
      <p>Technical cookies are used throughout your browsing session to facilitate it and to perform certain functions. A technical cookie may, for example, be used to remember the answers filled in a form or the user's preferences regarding the language or presentation of a website, when such options are available.</p>
      <p>Advertising cookies may be created not only by the website the user is browsing, but also by other websites serving advertising, ads, widgets or other elements on the displayed page. These cookies may notably be used for targeted advertising, i.e. advertising determined by the user's browsing.</p>
      <p>We use technical cookies and advertising cookies. They are stored in your browser for a period that cannot exceed six months.</p>
      <p>We use, or may use, audience analysis tools which generate a cookie measuring the number of visits to the site, the number of page views and visitor activity. Your IP address is also collected to determine the city you connect from. The retention period of this cookie is stated in section 6 of this policy.</p>
      <p>As a reminder, you can object to the storing of cookies by configuring your browser. Such a refusal could however prevent the site from working properly.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="consentement">
      <h2>12. Consent</h2>
      <p>When you choose to provide your personal data, you expressly consent to its collection and use in accordance with this policy and with the legislation in force.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="donnees">
      <h2>13. Access to your personal data</h2>
      <p>In accordance with French law no. 78-17 of 6 January 1978 on information technology, files and civil liberties, you have the right to obtain the communication and, where applicable, the rectification or deletion of the data concerning you, through online access to your file. You may also contact:</p>
      <p>email address: pierre@izika.com<br />postal address: IZIKA SAS – 199 rue Hélène Boucher – 34170 Castelnau-le-Lez, France.</p>
      <p>As a reminder, any person may, on legitimate grounds, object to the processing of data concerning them.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="modifications">
      <h2>14. Changes</h2>
      <p>We reserve the right, at our sole discretion, to change this policy at any time, in whole or in part. These changes take effect upon publication of the new policy. Your use of the site after these changes take effect constitutes acknowledgement and acceptance of the new policy. Otherwise, and if the new policy does not suit you, you must stop accessing the site.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="date">
      <h2>15. Effective date</h2>
      <p>This policy came into force on 05/12/2017.</p>
    </section>
  </LegalShell>
</StandardLayout>
